    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d656">

                <pb facs="0647" n="641" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg641"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Baron
                            Ketteler.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-07-11"><hi rendition="#italic">July 11,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 7th instant, in which you inform me that Mr. Greiner,
                    chancellor of the German consulate at Sydney, who has been provisionally
                    designated to act as the German member of the Samoan land commission, has
                    arrived at Apia, and that he entered upon the duties of the office on the 1st of
                    April last.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John W. Foster.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
